## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical design choices for document retrieval: chunking strategy, embedding/model trade-offs, vector DB indexing, and maintaining citations under updates.

## Key Concepts
- Chunking strategy and overlap
- Embedding model choices
- Vector DB indexing and freshness
- Passage citation and provenance
- Ingestion and incremental updates
- Evaluation: recall@k and latency

## Code Example
```javascript
// ingest
function chunk(text, size=1000, overlap=200){ /* ... */ }
const chunks = chunk(pdfText);
const embeddings = await Promise.all(chunks.map(c => embed(c)));
vectorStore.upsert(chunks.map((c,i)=>({id:`c${i}`, text:c, emb:embeddings[i]})));

// query
const qemb = await embed(userQuery);
const top = vectorStore.query(qemb, {topK:3});
const ranked = rerankWithCrossEncoder(top, userQuery);
return ranked.map(p => p.citation);
```

